It's been a lot of fun working for you, Mr. Lewis, and you've been a wonderful sponsor.

00:18:36.330 --> 00:18:40.000
And after all, where else can you find a comedian as funny as I am?

00:18:47.630 --> 00:18:50.270
Now, Mr. Lewis, I do think...

00:18:50.270 --> 00:18:51.930
I have the options you wanted to sign today.

00:18:52.090 --> 00:18:53.150
Oh, the options.

00:18:53.550 --> 00:18:55.090
Good, good, that's splendid.

00:18:55.270 --> 00:18:55.550
The options.

00:18:57.580 --> 00:18:59.900
Now, what is the first one?

00:19:00.090 --> 00:19:00.890
The first one.

00:19:01.090 --> 00:19:02.390
The Hit Parade.

00:19:02.470 --> 00:19:03.230
The Hit Parade.

00:19:04.240 --> 00:19:05.000
Anne Southern.

00:19:05.440 --> 00:19:06.700
There's Anne Southern's option.

00:19:07.540 --> 00:19:08.420
Robert Montgomery.

00:19:08.900 --> 00:19:09.540
Robert Montgomery.

00:19:09.760 --> 00:19:12.400
Now, you'll see these are put in the mail, so they can be countersigned.

00:19:12.420 --> 00:19:12.860
Yeah, but where's mine?

00:19:13.020 --> 00:19:13.240
Yes, sir.

00:19:13.760 --> 00:19:15.260
Well, I know, but where's my option?

00:19:15.760 --> 00:19:18.780
But my option, my option, look it, I came up here to sign an option.

00:19:19.040 --> 00:19:22.900
I mean, let's get this over with, Mr. Lewis, let's have no loose ends.

00:19:32.240 --> 00:19:34.320
Mr. Lewis, I said, let's have no loose ends.

00:19:35.020 --> 00:19:36.380
Jack, what are you looking for?

00:19:36.540 --> 00:19:37.680
You know what I'm looking for.

00:19:37.940 --> 00:19:38.880
Groucho told me.

00:19:39.920 --> 00:19:42.340
Look, Mr. Lewis, where's my contract?

00:19:42.520 --> 00:19:43.980
I came up here to sign a contract.

00:19:44.260 --> 00:19:44.640
Now, where is it?

00:19:44.820 --> 00:19:45.620
My desk alone.

00:19:45.860 --> 00:19:47.440
But it should be in the...

00:19:51.910 --> 00:19:56.490
Mr. Lewis, what is my contract doing in the wastebasket?

00:19:57.020 --> 00:19:58.480
It must have blown off my desk.

00:19:58.640 --> 00:19:59.960
You see, when the windows open, there's a...

00:20:00.090 --> 00:20:08.090
strong wind from the northeast. That's funny. Last year it was from the southwest. Look at

00:20:08.090 --> 00:20:14.360
Mr. Lewis. Now, why beat around the bush? I mean, everything we say here is, we're pride

00:20:14.360 --> 00:20:19.150
we're in here alone. I mean, there's nobody else in here but us. Jack, regretting your

00:20:19.150 --> 00:20:24.350
option. What? I mean, regarding your option. Yes, yes, yes. I must have a little time

00:20:24.350 --> 00:20:29.970
to think it over. But I can't understand why you're hesitating, Mr. Lewis. I mean,

00:20:30.220 --> 00:20:33.580
I don't know, something tells me that you must have someone else in mind.

00:20:34.060 --> 00:20:37.880
And I don't know why you keep doing that to me.

00:20:38.040 --> 00:20:41.500
After all, I've been with the American Tobacco Company for a long time,

00:20:41.520 --> 00:20:44.010
and I'm not as young as I used to be.

00:20:44.840 --> 00:20:47.420
That's true. You were 39 when you joined us.

00:20:48.000 --> 00:20:48.600
That's right.

00:20:49.130 --> 00:20:52.990
And I've done a great job all these years, Mr. Lewis, for the American Tobacco Company.

00:20:53.520 --> 00:20:56.720
I don't know, I've worked hard, we've had wonderful shows,

00:20:57.300 --> 00:20:59.240
and I've sold the product.

00:21:00.000 --> 00:21:05.300
Twice, I let you exercise the tobacco-picking clause.

00:21:05.900 --> 00:21:07.940
We didn't exercise it. You held us to it.

00:21:09.340 --> 00:21:12.200
Well, I still can't understand why you're doing it.

00:21:12.340 --> 00:21:14.180
There's some reason why you're stalling.

00:21:14.900 --> 00:21:17.000
Jack, you're taking the wrong attitude.

00:21:17.450 --> 00:21:20.430
I haven't come to any decision about dropping your option.

00:21:20.590 --> 00:21:23.850
It's just that I want to think it over for a while,

00:21:23.970 --> 00:21:25.830
just for, say, four or five days.

00:21:28.200 --> 00:21:28.520
Well.

00:21:30.440 --> 00:21:42.690
all right i'll i'll wait uh four four or five days yeah that's right jack now where can i get

00:21:42.690 --> 00:21:48.670
in touch with you well just call your secretary i'll be sitting in the outer office but don't

00:21:48.670 --> 00:21:49.290
Don't forget now.

00:21:49.530 --> 00:21:49.930
Don't forget.

00:21:50.170 --> 00:21:51.450
Oh, you got the wrong...

00:22:00.800 --> 00:22:04.900
Fred! Fred, what are you doing in that closet?

00:22:05.330 --> 00:22:07.230
Believe it or not, I'm playing post office.

00:22:08.250 --> 00:22:09.790
Post office? Kiss me.

00:22:12.730 --> 00:22:16.550
But Mr. Lewis, there's something fishy going on here,

00:22:16.570 --> 00:22:18.150
and I'm going to get to the bottom of this.

00:22:18.680 --> 00:22:20.260
What's Fred Allen been telling you?

00:22:20.630 --> 00:22:22.090
Jack, there's no need to get excited.

00:22:22.530 --> 00:22:25.050
You know the entertainment business is very competitive.

00:22:25.820 --> 00:22:27.970
Oh, so it's competitive, huh?

00:22:28.440 --> 00:22:29.140
So that's it.

00:22:30.510 --> 00:22:33.980
Fred Allen, you ought to be ashamed of yourself,

00:22:34.620 --> 00:22:37.020
coming in here and trying to get my job away from you.

00:22:37.100 --> 00:22:38.780
Well, gee, Jack, I had to do something.

00:22:39.060 --> 00:22:40.840
I've eaten so much of that dog food,

00:22:40.860 --> 00:22:43.040
they've written a song about me being in a window.

00:22:46.980 --> 00:22:49.500
Well, I still say you ought to be ashamed of yourself.

00:22:49.520 --> 00:22:51.520
Well, I guess I am a heel, Jack.

00:22:51.760 --> 00:22:56.940
But always remember, next to a heel, you always find a good soul.

00:22:57.360 --> 00:22:59.890
And I'm quoting from that famous poet, Tom.

00:23:00.000 --> 00:23:09.630
McCann. After that awful joke, I shouldn't forgive you, but I will, because I know you

00:23:09.630 --> 00:23:13.840
didn't mean it. Well, okay, Fred, now listen, let's forget all about it. We'll go out and

00:23:13.840 --> 00:23:22.490
have a cup of coffee. Don't forget to send for me. I thought they'd never leave.

00:23:32.140 --> 00:23:34.760
Now that they've gone, let's talk business.

00:23:35.130 --> 00:23:37.690
What do you want with Fred Allen? What do you want with Jack Benny?

00:23:37.890 --> 00:23:40.630
With me, you've got a young man who can sing, who can dance,

00:23:40.940 --> 00:23:43.580
who clocks his hands, rolls his eyes, and I'm so friendly.

00:23:43.700 --> 00:23:45.500
Mr. Lewis, you'd never regret it.

00:24:00.860 --> 00:24:04.540
We'll be back in just a moment, but first, a word from Dorothy Collins.

00:24:05.170 --> 00:24:10.880
Very much, ladies and gentlemen.

00:24:11.040 --> 00:24:14.620
Naturally, we were only kidding about my sponsor not picking up my option

00:24:14.620 --> 00:24:18.860
because I am signed with the American Tobacco Company until I am 40.

00:24:20.300 --> 00:24:23.350
They didn't know what they were getting into.

00:24:24.410 --> 00:24:28.240
Oh, Fred, Fred Allen, come on out here, will you, Fred?

00:24:33.000 --> 00:24:35.620
It's really been nice having you on the show, and you were wonderful.

00:24:35.740 --> 00:24:38.820
Well, Jack, you won't believe this, but I tried to louse the whole thing up.

00:24:39.360 --> 00:24:40.260
I believe it.

00:24:40.560 --> 00:24:41.060
I believe it.

00:24:41.460 --> 00:24:44.340
But, Fred, let me ask you, is there any truth to that about eating the dog food?

00:24:44.500 --> 00:24:44.880
Oh, yes.

00:24:45.000 --> 00:24:46.180
Three times a day, I have it.

00:24:46.540 --> 00:24:48.040
Well, doesn't it upset your stomach?

00:24:48.260 --> 00:24:52.860
Well, no, it doesn't bother my stomach, Jack, but eating out of the bowl is hot on my knees.

00:24:53.600 --> 00:24:57.520
I see.

00:25:01.020 --> 00:25:03.040
Eddie, Eddie Tanner, come on out.

00:25:09.540 --> 00:25:14.560
I want to tell you, it was just wonderful you to come in here just to do this one little bit on the show.

00:25:14.700 --> 00:25:16.380
Jack, I want to tell you, it was my pleasure.

00:25:16.560 --> 00:25:18.140
No, no, no, no, Eddie, it was my pleasure.

00:25:18.300 --> 00:25:20.260
Believe me, Jack, it was my pleasure.

00:25:20.440 --> 00:25:25.680
Eddie, ladies and gentlemen, this shows you what happens when two straight men get together.

00:25:28.100 --> 00:25:28.940
What did you say, Fido?

00:25:32.110 --> 00:25:34.710
Now give me my red hot and let me get out of here.

00:25:35.700 --> 00:25:37.020
No, listen, I'll tell you what.

00:25:37.280 --> 00:25:39.400
You fellas have been such good sports.

00:25:39.400 --> 00:25:40.440
I'll tell you what I'm gonna do.

00:25:40.560 --> 00:25:42.660
I'm gonna invite you both to my house to dinner tonight

00:25:42.660 --> 00:25:43.840
and I want you to bring your wife.

00:25:44.260 --> 00:25:45.000
Oh, that's nice.

00:25:45.320 --> 00:25:47.200
Jack, Jack, I've never been to your house.

00:25:47.300 --> 00:25:48.000
How do you get there?

00:25:48.290 --> 00:25:49.030
Oh, that's right.

00:25:49.190 --> 00:25:51.110
Well, look, you go two blocks.

00:25:51.150 --> 00:25:51.910
You're covering me.

00:25:52.210 --> 00:25:52.670
Oh, oh, pardon me.

00:25:58.580 --> 00:25:59.960
You go, Eddie, let...

00:26:00.000 --> 00:26:01.500
Fred, you're ready.

00:26:01.600 --> 00:26:02.220
My name is Sam.

00:26:03.180 --> 00:26:04.800
This is Fido.

00:26:04.900 --> 00:26:05.700
No, Chad, Fred.

00:26:06.980 --> 00:26:07.600
Look at this.

00:26:07.960 --> 00:26:08.620
You go two...

00:26:08.620 --> 00:26:09.600
You want to know how to get to my house?

00:26:09.720 --> 00:26:09.820
Yeah.

00:26:09.820 --> 00:26:11.580
Now, you go two blocks to your right

00:26:11.580 --> 00:26:14.060
till you come to the California Bank.

00:26:14.180 --> 00:26:14.840
California Bank.

00:26:15.080 --> 00:26:16.880
Then you go four blocks to your left

00:26:16.880 --> 00:26:18.500
till you come to the Bank of America.

00:26:18.620 --> 00:26:19.280
Bank of America.

00:26:19.520 --> 00:26:21.260
Then seven more blocks to the right

00:26:21.260 --> 00:26:23.560
till you come to the Citizens National Bank.

00:26:23.760 --> 00:26:23.940
You see?

00:26:24.320 --> 00:26:25.120
Then you keep going.
